<title>CROATIA: Croatian Oct oil output rises, natural gas falls.</title>
<headline>Croatian Oct oil output rises, natural gas falls.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Central Bureau of Statistics issued the following oil and natural gas output details.</p>
<p> CROATIA OIL EXTRACTION     OCTOBER     SEPTEMBER     OCT '95</p>
<p> Crude oil	 (tonnes)   142,173	115,763	125,902</p>
<p> Natural gas (000 cu m)     150,361	156,485	173,568</p>
<p> OIL PRODUCTS (tonnes)</p>
<p> Gasoline			  76,142	 69,703	 47,379</p>
<p> Gas oil			   60,851	 17,927	 25,552</p>
<p> Heating oil		    136,000	116,601	136,194</p>
<p>NOTES -- Data exlude production from oilfields in Serb-held Eastern Slavonia which was partly restarted late in August. -- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
